<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rose of Lima</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1586–<a href="/years/1617">1617</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Saint Rose of Lima, Isabel Flores de Oliva</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rose of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> was a Peruvian lay member of the Dominican order known for her severe asceticism, prayer and care for the poor and sick of Lima. Canonised by Pope Clement X in 1671, she was the first person born in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> to be declared a saint. She is the patron saint of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, of the Americas and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rose-of-lima.jpg" alt="Rose of Lima" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Claudio Coello · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sta_Rosa_de_Lima_por_Claudio_Coello.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
